otable if they have widespread (national or international) impact and were very widely covered in diverse sources, especially if also re-analyzed afterwards\"\". The Chicago protests were covered internationally (e.g.: http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/election-us-2016-35791008 BBC; http://www.swissinfo.ch/eng/trump-blames--thugs--for-cancelled-chicago-campaign-rally-/42016234 Swissinfo; http://www.asahi.com/articles/ASJ3D44FVJ3DUHBI015.html Asahi Shinbun), and have also been the subject of specific continued re-analysis (http://thefederalist.com/2016/03/14/in-defense-of-trumps-chicago-protesters/ \"\"In Defense of Trump's Chicago Protesters\"\" from today; http://theweek.com/articles/612481/liberal-protesters-didnt-stop-donald-trump-chicago-helped \"\"Liberal protesters didn't stop Donald Trump in Chicago. They helped him.\"\", likewise today\" [[User:Nizolan]] 20:13, 14 March 2016 (UTC)",
