could-accelerate-autopilot-development/ this from Ars Technica, https://web.archive.org/web/20191004024354/https://observer.com/2019/10/tesla-elon-musk-acquire-self-driving-startup-deepscale-autopilot/ this from the Observer, https://web.archive.org/web/20191101221238/https://www.engadget.com/2019/10/01/tesla-buys-deepscale/ this from Engadget and https://web.archive.org/web/20191014140528/https://www.cnet.com/roadshow/news/tesla-deepscale-autonomous-self-driving-tech/ this from cnet are all entirely based on the announcement that the company was being acquired by Tesla. All reference the CNBC announcement and the CEO's LinkedIn \"\"announcement\"\". The information about the company is clearly attributable to a source affiliated with the company and there is no \"\"Independent Content\"\". They all fail \" [[User:HighKing]] 14:09, 8 November 2019 (UTC)\n* article is written very much from insider's POV and borders on . The Tesla acquisition just gets it over the line in terms of notability, but I could see this comping up for deletion at a later point to be merged into the Tesla article [[User:Goldsztajn]] 15:05, 4 November 2019 (UTC)\n* \"Delete''' After reviewing references and searching online, I cannot locate sufficient references that meet the criteria for establishing notability. Existing references appear to be based on announcements or research from the company or connected companies, inclusion in \"\"Top 10\"\" type lists, quotations/interviews with people connected to the company and primary sources. Topic fails GNG and . There are multiple sources that provide Independent Content and meet the criteria for establishing notability, passes GNG/NCORP\" [[User:HighKing]] 15:49, 26 October 2019 (UTC)\n* per DGG and 104gli. Passes . An SNG can not override GNG [[User:4meter4]] 15:58, 3 November 2019 (UTC)",
